# `app_state` lock — UI deadlock

Canonical: `docs/DEV.md` bug **7a**.

## Fact (gdb, Khaynjo 2026-11-03)

Hung process: main thread on `futex_do_wait` / `Mutex::lock` of `app_state::STATE` inside `set_status_line_only` ← `set_status` ← Settings Bill/place tap.

Not wrap/Fill spam (that is bug 7; different signature: draw-time / high log volume).

## Forbidden

```rust
self.set_status(cx, app_state().lock().unwrap().t("…"));
self.set_status(cx, app_state().lock().unwrap().t("…").replace(…));
```

The temporary `MutexGuard` lives for the whole statement. `set_status` locks again → same-thread deadlock → OS “Not Responding”.

## Required

```rust
self.set_status(cx, app_t("…"));
// or
let msg = { let st = app_state().lock().unwrap(); st.t("…").replace(…) };
self.set_status(cx, msg);
```

`app_t` is in each app’s `runtime.rs`. Duplicate the same fix per app — no shared core.

Before claiming a Settings hang is wrap/Fill: dump stacks (`futex` + `app_state::STATE` vs turtle/draw).

## Named guards and repaint helpers (Khaynjo 1.0.0–1.0.4, 2026-11-10)

`sync_chrome` called `self.paint_frequent_config(cx)` while its `let st = app_state().lock()…` guard was live. That helper locks `app_state` itself, and it runs from `handle_startup`, so every launch froze before the first window on Windows, Linux and Android: no crash, no panic, ~0.4 s CPU, one more frozen process per icon click. On Windows it looked like a "dead icon" and cost five MSI rebuilds chasing shortcuts / stack size / installer repair. Proof: minidump of the hung PE (`Mutex::lock_contended` ← `paint_frequent_config` ← `sync_chrome`) and gdb on Linux (same frames, `match_event.rs` `handle_startup`).

- Call any `self.paint_*` / `self.sync_*` / `self.show_*` / `set_status` / `go` only after `drop(st)` or outside the guard's block (`paint_choice_pair` is the one exempt helper — it never locks).
- Each app's `scripts/check-lock-guards.sh` flags this, and `load_kumkaj_env` (every dev run and package, incl. `msi.sh`) now runs it and **stops the build** on a flag. `KUMKAJ_ALLOW_LOCK_GUARD_FLAGS=1` is for a confirmed false positive only.
- A windowless app that stays running after a launch is a hang, not a crash: capture the main thread's stack before changing installers.
